{
  "version": 3,
  "template": "blob",
  "space": "delta",
  "comment": "Troupe's clip library for the blob skeleton -- the amorphous archetype. Local joint rotations, XYZW. space=delta means each value is a rotation from the bone's own REST orientation, not the pose editor's node-local frame -- see blender_worker.POSE_SPACES. Every value was computed from a world-axis angle and converted through the bone's rest frame (basis = rest^-1 * R * rest). A POSE CARRIES NO SCALE, so squash and stretch are authored as rotation plus root_translation and nothing else: the four equator lobes swing down-and-out while the body sinks (squash) or are drawn up-and-in while it rises (stretch), and the base/core/crown/top column leans into the direction of travel. That is the honest limit of the format -- a blob that genuinely flattened would need a scaled bone, which no clip can carry -- and the lobes are in the template for exactly this. walk is a hop cycle rather than a gait, because a blob has no legs to put down in an order: squash, launch, float, land, with the travel in root_translation (character-height units). attack coils, surges up past the rest crown and throws the front lobe over the target, which is what an engulf reads as at 64 pixels.",
